SUMMARY:Balyasny Asset Management Coding Challenge
LOCATION:Lewis Library\, Room 120
DESCRIPTION:Test your skills on real problems from a multi-strategy hedge
  fund. Balyasny Asset Management (BAM) is hosting an invite-only coding 
 challenge at Princeton for students interested in technology\, data\, qu
 antitative trading\, and research. What to expect: - A hands-on technica
 l assessment that takes about 70 minutes. - Problems drawn from BAM's op
 en-source GitHub repository. They involve manipulating data sets and app
 lying math and statistics\, like the work BAM teams do. - A virtual mach
 ine for each participant. You can code in any language you like. - Cater
 ing and swag. - After the event\, BAM's team will review submissions and
  identify top performers.\nRegister: https://princeton.joinhandshake.com
 /edu/events/2044901\nhttps://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/baly
 asny-asset-management-coding-challenge
URL:https://careerdevelopment.princeton.edu/events/balyasny-asset-managem
 ent-coding-challenge
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
